# Forja pack-product host (non-negotiable)

Index: [community-owned plugins](./forja-plugins-community-owned.mdc) · [external plugins vs host](./forja-external-plugins-host.mdc) · [design system](./forja-design-system.mdc) · [RFC-109](../../docs/rfc/109-[open]-forja-pack-product-host.md)

**One-liner:** The app is an empty shell + engines. Packs are product. Foundation is a design system (paint only). Packs call `ctx.host` / `runPlugin` — they do not live in Dart.

**Community-owned plugins** = host does not know pack ids.  
**Pack-product host** = host does not own product UI.  
**Foundation** = tokens / primitives / components / widgets / protocol types — **not** an app kit orchestrator.

---

## Layers (locked)

| Layer | Path | Owns | Forbidden |
|-------|------|------|-----------|
| **Pack** | [forja-packs](https://github.com/mGhassen/forja-packs) `{hubs,providers,livesports,iptv,torrent}` | Product tabs, **layout JSON**, feed, prefs, chrome verbs, open shaping, portals product | Native unlock internals |
| **Host** | `apps/forja` | App frame (nav/settings/account/TV), **generic engines** (`runPlugin`, cache, store, vault, http, unlock, playback), **thin kit interpreter** that maps pack layout JSON → foundation widgets | Product screens, pack-id branches, hub/IPTV/Live/My List product folders |
| **Foundation** | `packages/forja_foundation` | Design system: tokens, theme, primitives, components, widgets, blocks, **protocol types** (layout JSON schema helpers) | `PackLayoutHost`, hooks, Riverpod session, registries, feed orchestration, product verbs |

```
Pack JS  →  layout / feed / actions  →  host engines + thin interpreter  →  foundation widgets (props only)
```

### Sniff tests

**Host file:** If this pack is uninstalled, does this Dart still make sense as a **generic capability**?  
- Yes → host  
- No → pack product in root — migrate or delete  

**Foundation file:** Would this belong in a shadcn-style design system (props in → UI out)?  
- Yes → foundation  
- No (hooks, registries, `runPlugin`, Riverpod kit session, PackLayoutHost) → **not foundation** — host engine or pack  

---

## Foundation is a design system — not a layout app

| Allowed in `forja_foundation` | Forbidden in `forja_foundation` |
|-------------------------------|----------------------------------|
| `tokens/`, `theme/`, `primitives/`, `components/`, `widgets/`, `blocks/` | `lib/layout/` orchestrators (`PackLayoutHost`, wire, feed chrome) |
| Protocol / layout **type** helpers (parse opaque JSON maps) | `*Hooks`, `*Registry`, Riverpod providers for catalog session |
| Props + callbacks only (RFC-095 / RFC-106) | Host bridges, fake `MetaRuntime`, product chrome verbs |

**Wrong:** parking kit runner / top-bar hooks / list registries inside the DS package.  
**Right:** DS paints `Button`, `PosterCard`, `TopBar`, `EpgGuide`, …; **host** interprets pack `layout` JSON and fills props from `runPlugin` results.

---

## Forbidden in `apps/forja`

| Do not | Why |
|--------|-----|
| Product folders `engine/hub`, `engine/lists`, `engine/live`, `features/iptv` | Root would know those products exist |
| `MetaCache` / catalog-meta-specific cache | Use generic `engine/cache` |
| Product `kit_*` screens under `shared/shell` | Paint in foundation; product in packs |
| `ctx.host.liveFeed` / product `myList` / product `iptv` / product `portals` namespaces | Use `cache`, `store`, `http`, `vault`, `plugin.run`, `playback.open` |
| Product boots (`KitLiveBoot`, IPTV core nav builder) | Pack `nav` only |
| Hardcoding pack ids / hub slots in host or foundation | Community-owned packs |

```
❌ shared/engine/hub/meta_cache.dart
❌ shared/shell/kit_top_bar.dart as product
❌ coreNavDestinations['iptv'] = IptvPtScreen
❌ ctx.host.liveFeed.load
❌ ctx.host.portals.searchChannels
❌ packages/forja_foundation/lib/layout/pack_layout_host.dart  (DS is not an app)
✅ shared/engine/cache/ + ctx.host.cache.*
✅ shared/engine/vault/ + ctx.host.vault.*
✅ ctx.host.http.request / playback.open / plugin.run
✅ pack layout JSON → host thin interpreter → foundation widgets
✅ live_sports → plugin.run(iptv hub, searchChannels)
```

---

## Allowed in `apps/forja`

- App frame: `shell/nav`, `shell/frame`, window, TV focus, account, settings shell
- Generic plugin runtime: install packs, `runPlugin(pluginId, action, params)`
- Generic cache / store / http / vault / unlock / playback open
- **Thin kit interpreter** (host engine): load pack `layout` / `feed`, map opaque widget types to foundation composers, zero pack-id product branches
- Boot hooks that register **opaque** verbs/sources from pack-declared ids — not product folders

---

## Packs tree (source of truth)

`forja-packs/{hubs,providers,livesports,iptv,torrent}` — not `plugins/live/**` or in-repo `plugins/hubs/**`.

Product development happens in **pack JS**. The app only offers engines; packs call them.
